# Fix-agent phase 6f (verify-report-phase-6.md SUGGESTION #2): makes the
# packages/core/pkg/ CRLF/LF contract explicit and version-controlled instead
# of resting entirely on every contributor's local `core.autocrlf` setting —
# the same reproducibility philosophy that motivated build-wasm.mjs's own
# host-path normalization (phase 4f, W1). `pkg/` is always fully REGENERATED
# by `pnpm run build:wasm` (never hand-edited), and wasm-pack's JS/TS codegen
# always emits LF regardless of host OS — these rules just make that an
# explicit, auditable guarantee so a Windows checkout's line endings can never
# silently diverge from what CI's drift check (`git diff --exit-code
# packages/core/pkg`) compares against on Linux.

# The compiled Wasm binary: never text-diffed, never line-ending-converted.
packages/core/pkg/*.wasm binary

# wasm-bindgen's generated JS/TS glue and its package.json: always LF, text
# diffable (useful for reviewing a pkg/ regeneration diff).
packages/core/pkg/*.js text eol=lf
packages/core/pkg/*.d.ts text eol=lf
packages/core/pkg/package.json text eol=lf
